    // megler-w10m: members added to the original's megler.Native (tools/build-framework.sh, "X.java.members").
    // The battery, asked of the core (hk_battery_read, core/src/run/hk_run.h), which is the one place that knows it: the
    // original's framework had a full battery written into the two classes that answer an app (megler.Broadcasts and
    // android.os.BatteryManager, both overlaid here to ask this instead).
    /** level, scale, status, plugged, health, millivolts, tenths of a degree Celsius, present (1 or 0): the numbers of Android's ACTION_BATTERY_CHANGED. */
    public static native int[] battery();
    /** The battery's kind as Android names it, "Li-ion". */
    public static native String batteryTechnology();
    /**
     * The frame meter (core/src/drivers/hk_java.c): 1 a frame begins, with its measure and layout; 2 its draw traversal begins; 3 it
     * has ended, having drawn `redrawn` pixels of the screen. Called by megler.ViewRoot.doFrame on the main thread.
     */
    public static native void frameMark(int phase, int redrawn);
